WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.950
New York City, 1970 to 1980.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.590
The whole city lost 10.4
per cent of its people.

3
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.930
But a group of its poorest
neighbourhoods lost 25.9 per cent:

4
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.730
about a quarter.

5
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.990
Jobs and services moved out, and
vacant homes were left behind.

6
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:22.630
Then, in the 1980s, those same
neighbourhoods began to grow again.

7
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.170
So who moved back in?

8
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.810
The families who had left?

9
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:27.550
New arrivals from abroad?

10
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:33.110
In this mission, you'll measure deprivation
with both economic and social indicators.

11
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:37.590
Then you'll judge who gained and who
lost as these neighbourhoods changed.

12
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.080
Your mission: find out who came back
to New York's poorest neighbourhoods.
